    "original_review_scope_verbatim": "Complete original Theorem4.19 with every domain/parameter/Abelian-differential condition and full universal-covering/monodromy/quotient argument. The genuinely needed predecessor constructions are extensive: small quantum period inversion and Cohn uniformization, big Milanov modular deformation with coefficient formulas, canonical-to-flat isomonodromic coordinates, the local lattice-parameter transition and spectral-curve uniformization. They are retained in full with their author proofs and the actual coefficient/composition appendix, rather than treating the final Weierstrass formula as a substitution exercise. Background definitions fix all named connections, LG data and convergence domains; established results retain author references. The small model and its deformations are one problem unit. Duplicate introduction result statements, historical/motivational discussion, and post-theorem speculative remark are excluded. Unused pst-node/authblk/tikz/xy/fancyhdr imports are omitted; no coded figures or diagrams occur in the source.\n\nNo mathematical refereeing or assistant-generated proof. Native source and corresponding saved publisher PDF are hash-bound. Fresh required XeLaTeX passes1–2 with existing cache and -no-shell-escape passed, followed by one documented stabilization pass3; the auxiliary bytes are stable and the rerun-label warning is gone. Final log has no undefined references/citations, missing glyphs, or overfull boxes. Nonfatal source math-font and PDF-bookmark math-token notices affect no visible author formula. The selected4.19 statement, parameter domain, Weierstrass difference, covering/nonvanishing/monodromy quotient proof and Abelian differential were compared with original publisher pages54–56 and rendered46–48. The long original coefficient/period/canonical-coordinate construction is copied in author order; every referenced formula/statement resolves. The saved native source exactly equals the .tex member of the saved publisher archive.\n",
